       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg. Doses that high risk severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life of about 30 to 50 hours would make the effects last.\n\nWas this a typo? Here are the usual options:\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily** is the standard starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily** is the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg by mouth once daily** is sometimes used for frail or elderly patients, or for patients on other antihypertensives.\n\nIf you confirm the dose you want, I'll enter it right away. If 50 mg is intentional, please tell me the clinical reason, and I'll add it as a note on the order. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
